{"title":"Pulmonary Function Technician Roadmap","role":"Pulmonary Function Technician","summary":"A Pulmonary Function Technician (PFT Technician) is an allied healthcare professional who performs and supports diagnostic tests that evaluate lung function and respiratory physiology.","facts":{"Current degree":"Allied Health Sciences (B.Sc / BPT / BOT / BMLT etc.)","Course":"Respiratory Care Technology"},"about":[],"intro":[],"horizons":[],"sections":[{"heading":"Career Overview","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"A Pulmonary Function Technician (PFT Technician) is an allied healthcare professional who performs and supports diagnostic tests that evaluate lung function and respiratory physiology."},{"type":"p","text":"The role is important in pulmonary medicine, respiratory-care departments, sleep centres, critical-care units, occupational health programs, and diagnostic laboratories."},{"type":"p","text":"Core responsibilities include:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Pulmonary function testing"},{"text":"Spirometry"},{"text":"Lung-volume testing"},{"text":"Diffusion-capacity testing"},{"text":"Bronchodilator testing"},{"text":"Peak-flow assessment"},{"text":"Patient preparation and coaching"},{"text":"Equipment calibration and quality control"},{"text":"Respiratory test documentation"},{"text":"Infection-control procedures"},{"text":"Supporting respiratory physicians in diagnostic evaluation"}]},{"type":"p","text":"The technician's primary responsibility is to obtain accurate, reproducible physiological measurements. Clinical interpretation and diagnosis are generally performed by appropriately qualified physicians or respiratory specialists."},{"type":"note","label":"Scope note","text":"Specific procedures and responsibilities vary by qualification, institution, employer and applicable regulations."}]},{"heading":"Career Horizon","kind":"horizons","blocks":[{"type":"table","header":["Stage","Primary Focus","Career Outcome"],"rows":[[{"text":"Year 1"},{"